From: SJ Park <sj@kernel.org>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 13:00:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ==== beyond a-bit milestone 2 ====

mm/damon: let users report their finding

TL;DR
=====

Let users report their finding of specific data attributes to DAMON.

DAMON collects data attribute information on its worker threads
(kdamond).  This restricts types of attribute information that DAMON can
monitor.  For example, it can know whether an access to a given memory
is made, using page table accessed bits.  But it cannot know by which
CPUs or tasks the access is made.  It cannot know if the access was for
a read or a write.  Kdamond-external kernel components such as perf
event overflow callback could know that.  The users could also know some
of such information.  But there is no way to safely and efficiently pass
the information to DAMON.

Allow users to provide such information.  For this, introduce data
attribute report system and add the user report support.

The report system allows any kernel space components in any context
including NMI context pass their finding to DAMON as a report.  For
this, define a data structure for such reports.  Implement and expose an
API function for submitting the report of the data type to DAMON.  The
submit function can be called from any context including NMI context.

Extend DAMON probe filter to work with the reports.  Introduce a new
filter type.  Filters of the type matches to a given memory if a report
of a given type for the memory is made in the last sampling interval.

Introduce a type of the report for user-provided report.  Extend DAMON
sysfs ABI to let users manually submit such report one by one for each
arbitrary address range of the memory.  Update the probe filter ABI for
the user-submitted report type.

In future, the report system will be extended and optimized for
kernel-space report producers.  Specifically, there is a plan to collect
read/write information with source CPU/task using perf event callback
based report producers.

